CPU(PPC) could never be defined.

The 32-bit PowerPC test asks for CPU(BIG_ENDIAN), which this same header
defines 230 lines further down, so it was always false and the build
stopped at "#error Unknown Architecture". The 64-bit tests above it ask
__BYTE_ORDER__ directly; this makes the 32-bit one match.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformCPU.h	2026-09-22 16:07:59
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformCPU.h	2026-09-22 16:08:13
@@ -90,7 +90,8 @@
     || defined(_M_PPC)         \
     || defined(__PPC))         \
     && !CPU(PPC64)             \
-    && CPU(BIG_ENDIAN)
+    && defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) \
+    && (__BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__)
 #define WTF_CPU_PPC 1
 #define WTF_CPU_KNOWN 1
 #endif
